Perry claims `node:readline` and `node:readline/promises`, but the current surface still mixes top-level exports with Interface instance members, leaves promise classes stubbed, and diverges on the core `question()` flow. This epic splits the readline work out of the broad #3795 utility bundle so an implementer can take the terminal/readline API end to end.

## Evidence

Baseline:
- Perry `origin/main@ffebfca51c97500a93074a4338241fc5e44b4fff` (`fix(node:fs): add disposable mkdtemp and path error parity (#3814)`)
- Release binary: `target/release/perry` from the current `origin/main` build
- Node runtime used for the probes: `v25.9.0`

Claimed API surface from `target/release/perry --print-api-manifest`:

```text
